          "title": "Identifying Singular Matrices"
        },
        "question": {
          ":question/id": "a042c4f3-05c8-5a87-8a50-0b2c7267b082",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $B$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "A square matrix is singular if and only if its determinant is zero.\n\nExpand along the top row, with signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(B) &= 0\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&\\quad +(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&\\quad +2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 0\\left(8-(-8)\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad +(-4)\\left(4-(0)\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad +2\\left(8-(0)\\right) \\\\\n&= 0\\cdot 16 \\\\\n&\\quad +(-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\\n&\\quad +2\\cdot 8 \\\\\n&= 0-16+16 \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(B)=0$, $B$ is singular.\n\nDo not select \u201c$\\det(B)=16$.\u201d\n\nDo not select \u201c$\\det(B)=-32$.\u201d\n\nSelect \u201c$B$ is a singular matrix.\u201d",
          ":question/answer-fields": [
