          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $D$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ - 4 \\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "A square matrix is singular if and only if its determinant is zero.\n\nExpand along the top row, with signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(D) &= \\sqrt{2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&\\quad +0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ - 4 \\sqrt{2} & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&\\quad +\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ - 4 \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}\\left(0-(2)\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad +0\\left(0-(- 8 \\sqrt{2})\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad +\\frac{1}{2}\\left(0-(- 4 \\sqrt{2})\\right) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&\\quad +0\\cdot 8 \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n&\\quad +\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n&= - 2 \\sqrt{2}+0+2 \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(D)=0$, $D$ is singular.\n\nDo not select \u201c$\\det(D)=-2 + 2 \\sqrt{2}$.\u201d\n\nDo not select \u201c$\\det(D)=2 \\sqrt{2}$.\u201d\n\nSelect \u201c$D$ is a singular matrix.\u201d",
